From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Merchant <john@johnmerchant.dev>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:19:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 45/45] hw/usb/hcd-imx21: Raise an unhandled ETD done again
 each frame

Linux's imx21-hcd handles an interrupt by reading SYSISR, walking all 32
ETDs for done status and then writing back the SYSISR bits it read on
entry. An ETD that completes while that walk is past it sets DONEINT
again, and the write-back clears it unseen; its ETDDONESTAT bit stays
set but no interrupt follows. The driver also masks the SOF interrupt
unless an ETD looks stuck, so the SOF the model kept raising for an
unhandled done never reached it either.

Starting ETDs on the next frame (an earlier fix) narrowed this, but the
walk can still span a frame boundary when the vCPU runs late against
the virtual clock. A keyboard's interrupt endpoint then went quiet after
a few keys, or a control transfer timed out during enumeration.

While an enabled done status is unhandled, each frame now raises
DONEINT as well as SOF, so a done whose interrupt was acknowledged
unseen is delivered on the next frame.

Signed-off-by: John Merchant <john@johnmerchant.dev>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B1fN5Fc77Z6fVVe4rWJxPT
---
 hw/usb/hcd-imx21.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hw/usb/hcd-imx21.c b/hw/usb/hcd-imx21.c
index e04ca4d1e..2a3e61a1d 100644
--- a/hw/usb/hcd-imx21.c
+++ b/hw/usb/hcd-imx21.c
@@ -494,8 +494,15 @@ static void imx21_usb_frame_tick(void *opaque)
 {
     IMX21USBOTGState *s = opaque;
 
+    /*
+     * While a done status is unhandled, raise the done interrupt again
+     * each frame, not just SOF. Linux's imx21-hcd acknowledges the SYSISR
+     * bits it read on entry to its handler, so a done raised while the
+     * handler runs is cleared unseen, and the handler keeps the SOF
+     * interrupt masked unless an ETD looks stuck.
+     */
     if (R(ETDDONESTAT) & R(ETDDONEEN)) {
-        R(SYSISR) |= SYSI_SOFINT;
+        R(SYSISR) |= SYSI_DONEINT | SYSI_SOFINT;
         imx21_usb_update_irq(s);
     }
     imx21_usb_process(s);
